WEBVTT

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:10.790
Where am I?

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.290
Hey, Rauna I!

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:13.890
No, no!

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.460
That doesn't go here! Bring it over there!

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.290
I'm sorry.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:29.540
Hey! You left out the mixer for the organic cement!

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:30.970
Have a Shio carry it!

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:33.370
It's all right; I'll do it myself.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.250
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:46.490
<i>Then we repeat, going</i>
<i>eternally round and round</i>

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:54.030
<i>Where will our path lead?</i>

00:00:54.030 --> 00:01:00.540
<i>What do I lose sight of when I'm with you?</i>

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:08.180
<i>A colorful array of love and kindness</i>

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:14.880
<i>I've remembered what</i>
<i>I'd forgotten since the days</i>

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:21.190
<i>when we hurt each other over trivial things</i>

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:28.460
<i>The sounds of our footsteps are</i>
<i>the "tracks" that lead to the future</i>

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:36.210
<i>Within the ever-changing scenery... always</i>

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:38.240
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.310
<i>Then we repeat, going</i>
<i>eternally round and round</i>

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:50.320
<i>This melody that paints the future,</i>
<i>until the world changes</i>

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.320
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:57.590
<i>The sun always rises again,</i>
<i>eternally repeating its arc</i>

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:08.440
<i>It lights up our path</i>

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.660
Are you okay, Violin?

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:29.460
What's wrong, Birdy? Hurry up and go to sleep.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.360
You're working day and night lately.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.830
I'm fine.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:35.130
But...

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:37.630
As soon as this translation is over...

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:40.630
Don't worry, Birdy. Okay?

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:43.860
Mm-hmm.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:53.020
Violin and Birdy were like a real mother and child.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.680
This is definitely strange.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.950
Huh?

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:58.150
Let's try correcting the data.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.300
What's?!

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.800
It appears Birdy's memories were
altered according to her own wishes.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.370
Especially the ones concerning Violin.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:17.170
Then the Violin I've seen so far was?

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.180
Violin was a sophisticated marionette,

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:25.480
but she was merely operating as
programmed to care for the lxioran.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:30.350
However, the young Birdy
was unable to accept that truth.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:34.760
She must've tried to convince herself
that Violin was the same as a person.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:39.760
The mentality of these
humanic races is truly illogical.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.370
We cannot comprehend them.

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:46.340
But <i>he's</i> a humanic too; what about him?

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.320
Nataru?

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.270
Hey, Violin.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.610
Let's play the game together!

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:59.880
He's here right now, so play with him, Birdy Cephon.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.710
You're so mean!

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.090
It's not her fault.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:06.420
I guess not.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:09.190
I know! Nataru, put out your hand!

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:11.020
Hurry up!

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:21.800
It's so warm! Your hand is warm and it feels nice!

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:24.870
Hey, Dad, what's that?

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:26.270
Just watch.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.720
It's a kilk!

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:37.420
You've been wanting one, right?

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.290
Thanks, Dad!

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:40.660
You like it, huh?

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:41.650
Yeah!

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.630
Birdy...

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:52.670
I'll come visit you any time you're lonely.

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:54.170
Really?

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:56.000
That's a promise, Nataru!

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:03.910
Today, on the second anniversary
of the tragedy at Acrabal,

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:07.910
a memorial ceremony is about
to be held at Central Tower.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:13.260
His Eminence Ley Signa, the Sanctum Sanctorum's
Divine Interpreter of the Seventh Seat,

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.830
will be delivering a eulogy,

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:18.630
- Wait up!
- and with the capital in a state of high alert,

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.530
- Stop that, Birdy, it's dangerous!
- a large audience including the mayor of Oriotera

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:25.160
- I'm fine!
- is gathered here in the Great
Circle, where the event will be held.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:35.040
Birdy!

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:37.270
Nataru!

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:44.690
Birdy!

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.220
Ow, ow, ow...

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:49.660
Are you okay, Birdy?

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:58.490
Sheesh, you're supposed to be an lxioran?
You're so clumsy.

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:02.000
Here.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.540
I messed up.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:07.510
Birdy.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:08.740
Tuto?

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:11.710
Birdy Cephon, you have emergency orders.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:13.480
Come with me right away.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:14.470
Dang it...

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:17.550
Instructor!

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:19.420
Did something happen?

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:21.060
Just get in.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:22.860
Yes, Sir.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:28.430
Megius contacted me and told
me that Violin is in the hospital.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:29.770
Violin?!

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:32.600
You didn't know?

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.570
Well, don't worry so much.

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:38.770
It's just a regular inspection
she has once every ten cycles.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:40.210
"Regular inspection"?

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:44.880
Yo, Nataru.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.850
Don't be so scared.

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:48.080
Valic...

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:51.590
It's nothing bad. Come with me for a sec.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:55.890
She's in a marionette specialty
facility inside Central Tower.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.090
There's nothing to worry about.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.050
Nataru...

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.970
Are we going to Central Tower?

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:12.370
Yes.

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:14.240
Violin is...

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:19.950
Stop worrying, Birdy. Violin was basically an excuse.

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:20.750
Huh?

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:24.490
It'll be a good experience for you
to watch the memorial ceremony.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:28.320
It's not the kind of thing you can see too often.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:36.170
Whoa...

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:39.440
Lots of curious onlookers here, huh?

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:42.240
It's so big, isn't it?

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:45.440
Don't judge just on appearances, Birdy.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:49.310
What's important isn't what's on the outside,
but what's on the inside.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:50.780
Yes, Instructor.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.520
Okay, shall we go take a look at the security?

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:54.680
Yes, Sir!

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:59.820
Today there are three mobile
patrol battalions deployed inside.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:02.020
- Wow, that's amazing.
- His Eminence Ley Signa of the Sanctum Sanctorum

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:04.330
- But more isn't necessarily better.
- His Eminence Ley Signa of the Sanctum Sanctorum

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.760
will be arriving shortly via warp.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:14.140
I'm a lucky robot doctor,
getting to run diagnostics on a Rauna I.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:16.370
Well? How is she?

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:21.510
Well, she's quite heavily used, so we
need to do some maintenance on her.

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:25.150
She's currently caring for an lxioran child.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:28.150
Make sure she's in perfect condition.

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.350
Just leave it to me.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:50.170
Birdy, this is the normal
equipment for the armed police.

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:51.840
Take a good look!

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.240
Yes, Instructor.

00:08:57.710 --> 00:08:58.750
It's me.

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:02.750
Chief, could you come to
the Great Circle's control room?

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:04.020
Is something wrong?

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:08.220
I'm not sure, but I'm told a
space-time disturbance has appeared

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:10.220
south-southwest of Central Tower.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:20.770
His Eminence has manifested himself.
Fixing coordinates.

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:28.410
Okay, that wraps up our observation.
Want to go pick up Violin, Birdy?

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:30.350
Yes, Instructor!

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:34.180
Megius should be with her, so we'll
all go watch the ceremony together.

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:36.420
Okay!

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:39.220
It's coming, Tsutomu.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.690
- Now listen up. The fundamentals of guard duty are...

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:42.560
- Birdy!

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.690
What's this?

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:44.390
What is it?

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:47.020
A warp hole's appeared! Sound the alarm!

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:55.470
What was that?

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:56.870
What happened?!

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:58.540
There are intruders in Area 8!

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:00.980
Intruders?!

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:02.140
Is this...

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:04.950
It's the moment the Central Tower terrorism happened.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:07.820
Tsutomu, you must not allow yourself to be upset.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:11.050
This is not reality. It's the past.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.130
The Great Circle is seriously damaged!

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:24.000
What happened?

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.270
We have intruders!

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:27.100
Contact guard headquarters!

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.570
Prepare to fire!

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:39.970
Fire!

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:52.160
Retreat! Retreat!

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:56.170
The guard company in Block 7 was wiped out?!

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:58.160
Give me the details on the intruders.

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:03.140
Federation Government,
hello again after two years.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:06.680
The Acrabal incident was unfortunate.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.010
Christella Revi?

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:13.680
However, you fools learned nothing.

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:16.020
For you to not only ignore my demands,

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:16.490
Neltz's company was wiped out?!

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:18.490
but try to justify that mistake with
this "memorial ceremony" farce...

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:20.490
The intruders are fanning out through the Tower!

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:22.120
Give me that thing!

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.130
Uh, Lieutenant Skeletso?!

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:23.860
Perhaps Acrabal was a bit too distant for you.

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:24.530
Birdy!

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:25.890
Yes, Sir!

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:29.470
You get out of Central Tower
right now and run as far as you can.

00:11:29.470 --> 00:11:29.700
Perhaps Huh?

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:30.300
So I thought to myself,
Huh?

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:32.230
So I thought to myself,
Birdy!

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:32.370
"What would happen if I did
the same thing here at Oriotera?"

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:33.970
Are you okay, Birdy?!

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:34.870
Yes...

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:38.240
Bastards...

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:38.670
Instructor?

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:39.410
Happily, this time I was
able to gain the cooperation

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:41.840
Something's there.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:43.250
That's...

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:43.880
Happily, this time I was
able to gain the cooperation

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:44.880
of others who shared my <i>aspirations:</i>
the Altan liberation front, Isdalta.

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.650
Don't get near them, you guys!

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:47.380
of othersThis way!

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:48.820
Hurry up!

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:50.090
of others who shared my <i>aspirations:</i>
the Altan liberation front, Isdalta.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:52.550
Undaunted by the persecution of Altans,

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:54.390
which has grown steadily fiercer since Acrabal,

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:55.920
which has grown steadily fiercer since Acrabal,
Those morons! I told them so!

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:58.030
Those morons! I told them so!

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:03.900
they rose up to make today the day we
strike down the corrupt Establishment,

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:06.600
and I hereby express my
deepest gratitude and respect.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:07.870
Instructor Skeletso!

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.510
Tuto, take care of Birdy!

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:09.710
My demands remain as <i>before:</i>

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:10.770
Instructor!

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:12.440
Birdy, this way.

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:15.910
that you cease all discriminatory
polices against Altans,

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:20.080
and that you grant planet Alta
independence from the Federation.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:21.280
They're here!

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:21.450
and that you grant planet Alta
independence from the Federation.

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:27.260
I hope you will use this solemn
ceremony as an opportunity

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:34.890
to reconsider your mistakes
and correct your thinking.

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.720
They're coming from behind!

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:45.040
Damn, they're just swarming everywhere!

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:46.480
Hurry up, men!

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:48.110
Skeletso! Are you all right?

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:51.580
Yeah. But there are too many of them.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:52.610
And Birdy?!

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:55.750
I tried to send her out of here with Tuto, but...

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:59.220
She's still inside Central Tower.

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:02.220
I can identify Birdy's current location.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:03.990
What?!

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:08.160
Shit. I should've gone with her after all.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:12.170
Violin, do you have data on these intruders?

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:17.110
They are Empire-era weapons called Berserker Units.

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:19.910
This is just from what my sensors can pick up,

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:22.850
but I believe they are headed for
the underground power reactor.

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:24.450
The underground power reactor?!

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:29.150
So they mean to blow up Central Tower?

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:30.750
Birdy is!

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:36.160
It's all right. I will save her without fail.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:37.990
Violin!

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:43.670
Happily, this time I was
able to gain the cooperation

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:49.670
of others who shared my <i>aspirations:</i>
the Altan liberation front, Isdalta.

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:53.280
Undaunted by the persecution of Altans,

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:57.480
which has grown steadily fiercer since Acrabal...

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:58.180
Tuto, which way should I go?

00:13:58.180 --> 00:13:59.520
Straight ahead.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.820
Okay, forward it is.

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:03.810
Oh, no, another one.

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:14.690
Dammit!

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:20.540
Above you, Birdy.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:21.970
Huh?

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:41.360
Birdy!

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:42.350
Tuto!

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:52.000
Birdy. Wake up, Birdy.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:52.990
Hey!

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:58.410
Tuto?

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.940
It's all right.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:02.280
There's no need to worry about me.

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:07.220
But the impact of breaking your fall
has slightly frozen my functions.

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:08.750
Can you be fixed?

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:10.950
Yes, I guarantee that.

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:14.760
Thank goodness. I wonder where we are?

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:17.930
We seem to have fallen to the lowest level.

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:22.120
So basically, we have to go up, right?

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:28.970
Hide, Birdy.

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:31.240
What are those guys doing?

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:34.110
They appear to be escorting something.

00:15:34.110 --> 00:15:38.310
Oh, I see. There's some
sort of unit controlling them.

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:41.540
What's that?

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:47.560
Birdy. Escape from here, quickly.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:48.550
Violin!

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:24.930
Violin?!

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:27.330
You mustn't come over here, Birdy.

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:48.670
Hurry and run, Birdy. I'll hold this off here.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:56.660
Violin!

00:16:56.660 --> 00:17:00.360
No, Birdy, it's too dangerous.

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:02.190
Violin!

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:43.070
B-Birdy...

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:46.060
Run... away...

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:49.110
Birdy...

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:08.450
Birdy... run...

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.060
Birdy!

00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:47.840
That's wrong!

00:18:47.840 --> 00:18:50.840
Run... Birdy...

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:52.270
That's wrong!

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:05.020
That thing isn't Violin!

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.010
That's wrong!

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:10.950
Birdy...

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:17.220
Birdy! Come on, wake up.

00:20:19.390 --> 00:20:20.590
Birdy!

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:28.200
Violin?

00:20:31.110 --> 00:20:32.330
Birdy.

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:43.110
Tsutomu?

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:47.390
Come on...

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:49.020
Let's go home.

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:05.640
Birdy has regained consciousness.

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:10.810
Yes, her neural entanglement
circuits are stable as well.

00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:15.040
The danger of mental fusion has been evaded for now.

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:19.090
Hey, Tsutomu.

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:24.930
Violin was a marionette, but she
protected me with her life, didn't she?

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:27.100
Yeah.

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:31.770
Even if she was just following
her programming as a machine,

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:33.960
I still care about her, even now.

00:21:39.010 --> 00:21:41.180
Birdy, can I ask you something?

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:42.180
What?

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:46.780
You once mentioned someone you'd like to see again...

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.920
Was it the man who saved you then?

00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:50.490
Yes.

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:54.290
I want to see him again and say "thank you."

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:56.660
But first...

00:21:56.660 --> 00:21:59.960
Thank you for saving me, Tsutomu.

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:02.950
Huh? Naw, I didn't really do much...

00:22:06.270 --> 00:22:11.110
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:22:11.110 --> 00:22:17.310
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:22:28.890 --> 00:22:34.400
<i>If you hang your head like that,</i>
<i>you won't get any sunlight</i>

00:22:34.400 --> 00:22:39.900
<i>Look up at the blue sky so you'll grow taller!</i>

00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:45.570
<i>Let's pour a few tears from the watering can</i>

00:22:45.570 --> 00:22:51.570
<i>Eventually shoots will spring up</i>
<i>from somewhere in your heart</i>

00:22:54.220 --> 00:22:57.320
<i>Let's take life slowly</i>

00:22:57.320 --> 00:23:02.320
<i>A girl's dreams are neverending</i>

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:08.560
<i>Ah, there's someone</i>
<i>out there waiting for you</i>

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:13.400
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:20.080
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:24.850
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:23:24.850 --> 00:23:30.840
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>
